# Extraction stub — QC-2009.04417

## Status
**Nougat OCR NOT run for this paper.** This file is a deferral stub, present for QC-100 artifact-set consistency.

## Rationale
- The paper is open-access (Quantum, CC-BY 4.0) with a clean, born-digital arXiv PDF (arXiv:2009.04417v4).
- Text was extracted with `pdftotext work/paper.pdf work/paper.txt` (see `work/paper.txt`).
- The `pdftotext` output was sufficient for claim enumeration (REPORT.md §2, 8 claims C1–C8) and for grep-based cross-checks against §3 (ZNE), §5 (PEC), §6 (CDR), Figs. 3–4.
- Nougat would add value if downstream analysis needed structured equation extraction (LaTeX ⇒ MathML) or table extraction, neither of which was required for the software-tool capability claim we replicated.

## If a real Nougat conversion is needed later
Run on any free-endpoint GPU host (e.g. uicgpu A100 or spark-36ac). Command:

```bash
# On uicgpu (recommended for A100 speed; ~2 min for a 30-page paper)
ssh uicgpu 'source ~/venvs/nougat/bin/activate && \
  nougat work/paper.pdf \
    --out extraction/ \
    --model 0.1.0-base \
    --no-skipping \
    --recompute'
```

Output would land at `extraction/paper.mmd` (Nougat's Markdown + LaTeX-math format). Move/rename to `extraction/nougat.mmd` for artifact-set consistency.

## Alternative if Nougat is unavailable
- `pdftotext -layout work/paper.pdf extraction/paper.layout.txt` for a plain-text fallback.
- `pdftohtml -s work/paper.pdf extraction/paper.html` for an HTML render (preserves layout + embedded images).

